remarks.para:
If you want your pages to handle the default method, you can either
            call the constructor like this:

            public class MyBasePage : MetaSapiens.PageMethods.BasePage
            {
              public MyBasePage() : base(true)
              {
              }
            }

            or create your own base page like this:

            public class BasePage : System.Web.UI.Page
            {
              protected override void OnLoad(EventArgs e)
              {
                base.OnLoad(e);
                if (!IsPostBack)
                  PageMethodsEngine.InvokeMethod(GetType(), this, true);
              }
            }

member.example:
If the following code is used:
[PageMethod(true)] void Test(int i, [Anchor] string a) { }
the corresponding URL for the following sample call: QueryMethods.Test(12, "myanchor") will be something like http://myserver/mypage.aspx?i=12#myanchor

If the following code is used:

[PageMethod(true), UrlFormat("~/{{METHOD}}{custID}.aspx")]
void EditCustomer(int custID)
{
}

The result URL would look like: http://myserver/myapp/EditCustomer12.aspx

summary.para:
A page method is managed by PageMethods:


a matching method that builds a URL will be generated;

this method will be invoked by PageMethods when a matching URL is used

member.example:
If the following code is used:
[PageMethod] void Test(int i) { }
the corresponding URL for the following sample call: QueryMethods.Test(12) will be something like http://myserver/mypage.aspx?PageMethod=Test&i=12

example.code:
void Application_BeginRequest(Object sender, EventArgs e)
{
  String url;

  url = Request.RawUrl;
  url = MetaSapiens.PageMethods.PageMethodsEngine.AddPostData(url, Request);
  Context.RewritePath(url);
}
